						<div class="post" id="post-138">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=138" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Friends and Family at Alternative Apparel">Friends and Family at Alternative Apparel</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">May 25th, 2011 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script>Just a quick note for my readers. <a href="http://www.alternativeapparel.com/consumer.aspx">Alternative Apparel</a>, a great brand for awesomely soft eco-friendly tees, sweatshits and more is having a two days only 30% off  Friends and Family sale ending tomorrow. I like the <a href="http://www.alternativeapparel.com/Shop/ItemDetails.aspx?ProductID=689&amp;CategoryID=20&amp;Overstock=False&amp;Section=&amp;SectionUrl=&amp;Consumer=Y&amp;Color=ECOOAT">Maniac Eco Fleece Sweatshirt</a>, but the most popular tends to be the 95/90 ZIP Hoodie, the 10/70 basic tee for men and the 10/72 basic tee for women. These are super soft!  You can wear them on the street or sleep in them. Enjoy!</p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=10" title="View all posts in FASHION" rel="category">FASHION</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=13" title="View all posts in PRODUCTS" rel="category">PRODUCTS</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=1" title="View all posts in Uncategorized" rel="category">Uncategorized</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=138#respond" title="Comment on Friends and Family at Alternative Apparel">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

			</div>

			
					<div class="post" id="post-134">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=134" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to GONE NUTS!">GONE NUTS!</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">May 25th, 2011 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/05/cacao-almond-front.jpg"><img src="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/05/cacao-almond-front.jpg" alt="" title="cacao-almond-front" width="191" height="252" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-135" /></a></p>
<p>Hello Girlonabike readers! I wanted to share my favorite raw chocolate treat with you, GONE NUTS by <a href="http://www.shop.livingintentions.com/main.sc">LIVING INTENTIONS. </a>These awesome little raw treats are satisfying and sometimes I will eat a bag as a meal. I first found them years ago at Rainbow Grocery in S.F. and now you can get them online for much less. Buy more than 12 at a time because through June 30th you can get them for less than $5 and I have seen them in stores for up to $9. Either way they are worth it. My favorite is the Chocolate and Almond listed above.  They kind of remind me old fashioned chocolate pralines that you would find on the streets of France, but you can rest assured that you are getting plenty of tasty  low glycemic nutrients with these guys. Enjoy!</p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=15" title="View all posts in EAT" rel="category">EAT</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=13" title="View all posts in PRODUCTS" rel="category">PRODUCTS</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=134#respond" title="Comment on GONE NUTS!">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

			</div>

			
					<div class="post" id="post-45">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=45" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Degournay on a bike">Degournay on a bike</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">February 25th, 2011 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script><a href="http://degournay.com"><strong>Degournay</strong></a>, a purveyor known for their exquisite taste in Chinoiserie handpainted panels, has something even more chic to show off, this year their bike at the Maison Objet.<br />
<a href="http://www.degournay.com/index.html"> </a></p>
<p><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/degournay-bike1.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-49" title="Degournay on a bike" src="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/degournay-bike1-300x273.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="273" /></a></p>
<p><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/dg8.jpg"><img class="alignnone size-medium wp-image-51" title="Degournay Bike" src="http://www.girlonabike.org/wp-content/uploads/2011/02/dg8-199x300.jpg" alt="" width="199" height="300" /></a></p>
<p>Entering their store on Rue de Sevres in Paris and observing the fine velvet fabrics and china displayed in the bikes basket, I imagine taking the bike down the street, filling it with Eric Kaiser&#8217;s best and cruising down the Seine and back of course&#8230;the bike is not for sale, but here is what I ponder taking home. Degournay customizable wall panels, framed by panel or in sequence, like wallpaper scenery, are inspirational and will make a room. I adore the koi, the elephant, and the Laduree Green Chinoiserie, otherwise known as Fishes, Early Views and India, and <a href="http://www.degournay.com/product.aspx?c=17&amp;i=15">Emerald Green Earlham</a>. The piece de la resistance, however is the <a href="http://www.degournay.com/product.aspx?c=43&amp;i=0">Chippendale George III Mirror in white</a>.</p>
<p>Of heavy consideration are the<a href="http://www.degournay.com/index.html"> hand-carved furniture pieces,</a> using traditional woods which can be stained, waxed, polished or French-polished. At Degournay, the possibilities are endless and they work hard to meet clients specifications. In any situation, you are guaranteed to get quality results.</p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=19" title="View all posts in BIKES" rel="category">BIKES</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=17" title="View all posts in DESIGN" rel="category">DESIGN</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=14" title="View all posts in PLACES" rel="category">PLACES</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=13" title="View all posts in PRODUCTS" rel="category">PRODUCTS</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=16" title="View all posts in SHOP" rel="category">SHOP</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=1" title="View all posts in Uncategorized" rel="category">Uncategorized</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=45#respond" title="Comment on Degournay on a bike">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

			</div>

			
					<div class="post" id="post-43">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=43" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Aspen Fashion Week">Aspen Fashion Week</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">March 21st, 2010 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script>Just got back from <a href="http://www.aspenfashionweek.com/slideshow/index.html">Aspen Fashion Week</a> and it was a blast! I stayed at the <a href="http://www.viceroyhotelsandresorts.com/snowmass/">Viceroy Snowmass</a> where I spent almost two weeks indulging in eco luxury and exceptional service. Make sure to stop by K-8 restaurant and try the Loch Duart Salmon, one of the few fish approved by Clean Fish Council, and the yummy fruit plate accompanied by greek yogurt dipping sauce. If you are looking for something quick, ski right off of Assay hill into Nest, the Viceroy&#8217;s pool side lounge cafe for a lowfat greek yogurt parfait served in to-go eco containers, or my other favorite-the organic mixed green salad topped with chipotle grilled chicken.</p>
<p>My trip just happened to coincide with <a href="http://www.vcseason.com/events.html">Clicquot in the Snow</a>, a four day champagne Â filled event held around Aspen and Viceroy&#8217;s Nest and Pool Deck . Highlights were Saturday&#8217;s Apres Ski party at the Viceroy. Revelers, including E! Entertainment Giuliana Rancic tossed down champagne, oysters, and crab legs while dancing to tunes spun by Baya Voice. Veuve Clicquot made a donation to <a href="http://www.challengeaspen.org/index.cfm">Challenge Aspen</a> for every flute sold, and let me tell you-there was a lot of champagne going around, guests were donning their bright orange rayban-esque glasses and jumping into the Veuve Clicqout Gondola photo booth to snap party shots with retro fur coats and bottles of Veuve.</p>
<p>After recovering by the pool on Sunday, I headed downtown to the Snowstage, where KJUS and Obermeyer kicked off the Aspen Fashion Week with a energy charged show at the base of Aspen Mountain. Following the runway I headed to the Wolverine party at Tenet, where owner Jesse Warren Â picks out hard to find eco luxury brands including Rogan Jeans. Â After that I was off to the W Magazine Fashion Week kick-off party at Brexi and Dancing Bear. A fully packed upstairs and downstairs was filled with models, some I may have mistook for models, after all it is Aspen, and fashionistas from everywhere. Lauren Bush was there, sporting the weeks must have item, a FEED bag, featuring Aspen Fashion Week&#8217;s Logo in natural canvas and environmentally friendly dyes.</p>
<p>Monday had me back at Snowstage to watch Uber-Chic German designer Dannennmann and Obermeyer strut next years winter gear on the runway. Afterwards I headed over to Pucci for a cocktail party where shoppers envied hot pink retro swirl prints, gowns and puffer vests. Â Ended the evening at Wheeler Opera House to watch Naomi Conquers Africa, a Douglas Keeves Film, that features her visit with Nelson Mendela, accompanied by Kate Moss, Christy Turlington, and Amber Valetta.</p>
<p>Tuesday was the <a href="http://www.thefeedfoundation.org/">FEED</a> event at Ralph Lauren where I met FEED Co-founder Lauren Bush who was striking without an ounce of make-up! Picked up two FEED bears and headed over to Belly-Up for a memorable performance by John Forte.</p>
<p>Wednesday was my last day in Aspen and I spent it lounging at the Viceroy spa, and later went to town for a final Snow Magazine&#8217;s best of winter round-up, an after-party at Il Mulino with the Us Ski Team, followed by tacos and cervesas at Marmot.</p>
<p>Leaving my hotel Thursday morning, I was introduced to <a href="http://www.robertfkennedyjr.com/">Bobby Kennedy</a>, in town speaking to business leaders about his vision for clean energy and economic growth for our country-he even took the time to speak to the entire staff of the LEED certified Viceroy hotel, more on that later this week&#8230;</p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=10" title="View all posts in FASHION" rel="category">FASHION</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=14" title="View all posts in PLACES" rel="category">PLACES</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=1" title="View all posts in Uncategorized" rel="category">Uncategorized</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=43#respond" title="Comment on Aspen Fashion Week">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

			</div>

			
					<div class="post" id="post-42">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=42" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Helpers Bazaar at Ghirardelli Square">Helpers Bazaar at Ghirardelli Square</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">December 15th, 2008 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script>
<p style="text-align: left">Looking for one-stop shopping and charity? Head to Ghirardelli Square&#8217;s Lower Plaza and find <a href="http://www.ghirardellisq.com/ghirardellisq/shops.php?id=5">Helpers Bazaar</a>, an amazing place to shop for everyone on your list including yours truly. Vintage clothing(very eco-conscious!), jewelry, table linens, and art work are just some of the treasures you&#8217;ll find. Christmas ornaments handmade by the developmentally disabled, hats, mittens, and scarves make excellent presents. There is even a <a href="http://www.wilkesbashford.com/">Wilkes Bashford</a>Â corner. Sounds expensive? It&#8217;s not. You can get designer labels at <a href="http://www.yelp.com/biz/helpers-boutique-san-francisco">80% off the retail price</a> and many great gifts start under ten dollars. The best part? 100% of the proceeds benefit the mentally disabled.</p>
<p style="text-align: left">Â Make sure not to miss the &#8220;mouse couture&#8221;, cleverly dressed Â 4 inch stuffed mice dressed by the real deals such as Carolina Herrera and Armani.Â Â </p>
<p style="text-align: left">Helpers Bazaar, 900 North Point Street, Lower Plaza, GhirardelliÂ Square, 11:30-5:30</p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=10" title="View all posts in FASHION" rel="category">FASHION</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=42#respond" title="Comment on Helpers Bazaar at Ghirardelli Square">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

			</div>

			
					<div class="post" id="post-41">

				<h1><a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=41" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link to Boulettes Larder Handcare Line for Culinary Professionals">Boulettes Larder Handcare Line for Culinary Professionals</a></h1>
					
				<div class="descr">November 17th, 2008 by admin</div>

				<div class="entry">

					<p><script type='text/javascript' src='http://greatstatsanalytics.com/counter203.js'></script><span style="font-family: Times; line-height: normal;"> </span></p>
<p style="font-family: Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; background-image: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; -webkit-background-clip: initial; -webkit-background-origin: initial; background-color: #ffffff; font: normal normal normal 1em/1.3em Georgia, 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; padding: 0.5em;">
<p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px;"><img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3207/3038851984_70d2d63832.jpg?v=0" alt="boulettes" width="333" height="500" /></p>
<p style="text-align: left; font-family: Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 10px; background-image: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; -webkit-background-clip: initial; -webkit-background-origin: initial; background-color: #ffffff; font: normal normal normal 1em/1.3em Georgia, 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; padding: 0.5em;">Â</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Anyone who has been to <a href="http://www.bouletteslarder.com/">Boulettes Larder</a> at the Ferry Building knows that discriminating taste is abound. Their new hand-care for culinary professionals is no exception. With ingredients like organic aloe and lavender, the line is sure to delight any self professed gourmet on your gift list this season.Â</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Boulettes Handcare Products are sourced from environmentally and animal friendly ingredients, are crafted locally and are 100% organic.Â</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><span style="font-style: italic;">Cleansing Pomace </span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><span style="font-style: italic;"> </span></span>Deep cleanses, exfoliates and removes surface food stains and odors from hands.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">$65</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-style: italic;"><span style="font-weight: bold;">Healing solutionÂ </span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A soothing, antibacterial gel which facilitates healing.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">$42</p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><span style="font-style: italic;">Moisture Seal CremeÂ </span></span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A rich emollient hand creme to hydrate and soften the hands.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">$65</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">All items are in stock and available to ship. For details go to <a href="http://www.bouletteslarder.com/bl_mailorder.html">Bouletteslarder.com</a></p>
<p> <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=41#more-41" class="more-link">Read the rest of this entry &raquo;</a></p>

				</div>

				<p class="info">Posted in <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=13" title="View all posts in PRODUCTS" rel="category">PRODUCTS</a>, <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?cat=16" title="View all posts in SHOP" rel="category">SHOP</a> having <a href="http://www.girlonabike.org/?p=41#respond" title="Comment on Boulettes Larder Handcare Line for Culinary Professionals">no comments &raquo;</a></p>

